The API client lives in ui2/frontend/src/auth/adminApi.ts and its helpers are one-liners over a shared call(), for example:

export function listDevices(): Promise<{ devices: DeviceSummary[] }> {
  return call("/devices", "GET");
}

The route this movement reads is GET /devices/{deviceId}/backups. Its response body is built by BackupController.toSummaryBody and carries exactly these keys, in this order: artefact_id, device_id, collected_at, size_bytes, digest_prefix, validation_level, deviation_state. The list is returned under the key "backups". deviation_state is null or one of exactly three values -- unchanged, changed, first -- enforced by a CHECK constraint in migration V18__cp_gateway_backup.sql. digest_prefix is already truncated by the server; it is a prefix, not a full digest.

Screens import shared pieces from ../shell/ScreenLayout (ScreenHeader, ListDetail, EmptyPanel, ScreenRoot), ../shell/M3Widgets (M3Button, M3Tabs, StatusChip) and ../shell/useFetchOnMount, and describe a failed request through a local describeApiError helper. InventoryScreen.tsx is the nearest example of all of these together.
